      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "Me4FDG, a polyhydroxylated glucose analog, does not cross the BBB in humans, illustrating that multiple polar hydroxyls can prevent CNS access; triptolide also carries several hydroxyls and epoxide oxygens, reinforcing the fail direction.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a polyoxygenated diterpenoid (triptolide-like) with multiple H-bond donors and epoxide oxygens. The most transferable direct evidence, Tanshinone IIB, shows poor brain penetration (~30% of plasma) due to P-gp/Mrp1 efflux, and the query's polar, efflux-prone scaffold is unlikely to achieve meaningful CNS access. Weak supportive nucleoside evidence does not override this.",
